ion (WO Strategy)", "body": "Adopt the Alfamidi playbook: rebrand viable compact storefronts and kiosks under the unified 'Hy-' master brand architecture (Hypermart & Hyfresh). Keep storefronts open to walk-in foot traffic while embedding dedicated GrabMart micro-fulfillment bays for 15-minute express deliveries.", "placement": "SWOT Matrix (WO Strategies); Brand Architecture"}, {"id": "FMX-06", "title": "Unified Loyalty & Digital App Ecosystem", "body": "Ensure all compact stores share the Hypermart Online app, WhatsApp Chat & Shop delivery, and OVO digital wallet points. Avoid creating separate sub-brand identities that confuse omnichannel shoppers.", "placement": "Omnichannel Strategy; Digital Integration"}]}, {"title": "Evidence & evaluation", "subtitle": "Portfolio fit and SWOT placement", "notes": [{"id": "FMX-07", "title": "Placement in SWOT Matrix", "body": "WT Strategy: Terminate non-core formats (SmartClub wholesale, unviable convenience leases) to plug the working capital deficit. WO Strategy: Scale Hyfresh as MPPA's distinctive, standardized residential fresh supermarket (mirroring Alfamidi's fresh network) with hybrid GrabMart O2O storefront integration.", "placement": "SWOT Matrix (WT-01 & WO-02 Strategies)"}, {"id": "FMX-08", "title": "Decision Criteria for QSPM", "body": "In the QSPM evaluation, evaluate whether capital should be spent trying to sustain multiple niche formats (FMX/Foodmart/Primo) versus aggressively rightsizing hypermarkets and scaling a single unified fresh format (Hyfresh).", "placement": "QSPM Decision Matrix (Strategy Prioritization)"}]}];

  const transmartBoardColumns = [{"title": "The Transmart Collapse", "subtitle": "Why higher revenue led to empty shelves", "notes": [{"id": "TM-01", "title": "The Working Capital Death Spiral & Supplier Boycott", "body": "Why Transmart's higher sales (Rp13.8T) were deceptive: Cash-flow strain from expensive mall entertainment builds forced Transmart to stretch trade payables beyond 90\u2013120 days. Unpaid FMCG and fresh food suppliers halted deliveries, leaving display chillers and grocery aisles completely bare across Jakarta and regional cities.", "placement": "SPACE Matrix (Defensive Position); CPM Rival Analysis", "source": "Case Exhibit 5; Industry Disclosures & FMCG Supplier Audits"}, {"id": "TM-02", "title": "The '4-in-1' Mall Entertainment Trap", "body": "Transmart committed immense capital to 8,000\u201312,000 m\u00b2 mega-stores integrating Trans Studio Mini indoor roller coasters and cinemas. When COVID-19 mobility curbs and mall restrictions hit, family leisure footfall plummeted. Unavoidable PSAK 73 non-cancellable mall leases and crushing air-conditioning/electricity overhead crippled operating cash flows.", "placement": "PESTLE Analysis (Economic & Social); Five Forces", "source": "Case Exhibit 4; CT Corp Retail Disclosures"}, {"id": "TM-03", "title": "Post-Carrefour Brand Equity Erosion", "body": "Following the buyout of Carrefour by CT Corp, the rebranding to Transmart alienated traditional value-conscious grocery shoppers. Transmart was widely perceived as overpriced without meaningful loyalty rewards. Once fresh produce shelves dried up, shoppers permanently defected to nearby minimarkets and supermarkets.", "placement": "Competitive Profile Matrix; Consumer Perception Benchmarks", "source": "Case p. 590; Retail Footfall Audits 2020"}]}, {"title": "MPPA's Cold-Chain Moat", "subtitle": "Why MPPA preserved a competitive posture", "notes": [{"id": "TM-04", "title": "Centralized 66,755 m\u00b2 Halal Cold-Chain Infrastructure", "body": "MPPA's core structural advantage is its 3 multi-temperature distribution centers (notably Balaraja and Surabaya). As the first Indonesian retailer with MUI Halal-certified cold-chain logistics, MPPA centrally manages farm-level chilling, temperature-monitored fleet transport, and automated cross-docking, maintaining fresh food quality standards that Transmart and minimarkets cannot replicate.", "placement": "IFE Matrix (Strength S2, score 4); SPACE CP (-3.20)", "source": "AR2020 Note 8; MUI Halal Logistics Certification"}, {"id": "TM-05", "title": "Protected Vendor Ecosystem & 'Champion of Fresh'", "body": "Unlike Transmart, MPPA protected its working relationships with 750 direct fresh food suppliers, ensuring uninterrupted daily shipments of produce and meats. Fresh food represented 24%+ of Hypermart sales and was non-discretionary, keeping shoppers returning for daily cooking essentials during lockdowns.", "placement": "IFE Matrix (Strength S1); SWOT SO-03 & ST-02 Strategies", "source": "Case p. 587; AR2020 Fresh Merchandising Review"}, {"id": "TM-06", "title": "Asset-Light Quick-Commerce Fulfillment (GrabMart)", "body": "Because MPPA had standardized chilled product staging and live SKU inventory, it swiftly converted 97 Hypermart stores into virtual dark stores on GrabMart, GoMart, and Shopee. Online sales jumped from 0.1% to 5% of revenue in 2020. Transmart had no equivalent digital infrastructure or chilled fulfillment capability.", "placement": "EFE Matrix (Opportunity O1); TOWS SO-04 Strategy", "source": "Case p. 594; e-Conomy SEA 2020 Report"}]}, {"title": "Strategic Takeaway & Defense", "subtitle": "Key arguments to defend during presentation", "notes": [{"id": "TM-07", "title": "Revenue Volume vs Operational Viability Defense", "body": "When asked why Transmart is Defensive despite having higher revenue (Rp13.8T vs Rp6.7T), explain that top-line scale is an illusion if supplier liquidity is broken. Transmart's negative X (-1.60) reflects a declining format with severed supplier trust, while MPPA's positive X (+0.60) reflects a viable fresh-food moat and agile omnichannel execution.", "placement": "SPACE Matrix Defense; Oral Defense Presentation", "source": "Fred David Strategic Management Ch. 6; Case Exhibit 5"}, {"id": "TM-08", "title": "Validation of MPPA's 2021\u20132025 Downsizing Strategy", "body": "Transmart's collapse validates MPPA's strategic decision NOT to pursue large-scale mall entertainment capex. Instead, MPPA must accelerate compact Hyfresh neighbourhood store conversions, monetize excess hypermarket square footage, and selectively close chronically cash-negative mall stores to avoid Transmart's fate.", "placement": "TOWS WT-01 & WT-02 Retrenchment; QSPM Matrix", "source": "Strategic Turnaround Plan 2021\u20132025"}]}];
