    "label": "Slide 6: Background of the study",
    "short": "Study background",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Study context · Financial baseline: 2020</div><h2>Background of the study</h2><div class=\"study-context-timeline\"><div><strong>2019</strong><h3>Existing profitability pressure</h3><p>MPPA entered the pandemic with an operating loss of Rp196.1bn.</p></div><div><strong>2020</strong><h3>Disrupted shopping patterns</h3><p>COVID-19 restricted mobility and operating hours. MPPA expanded online ordering, delivery and pickup as store visits weakened.</p></div><div><strong>2021–2025</strong><h3>The planning horizon</h3><p>The case asks how MPPA should allocate resources across its retail formats and channels to support recovery.</p></div></div><p class=\"study-context-link\">This study examines how MPPA can restore profitable sales while managing limited financial capacity.</p><div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: case pp. 587–590, 594 · AR2020 pp. 40, 54–55</span><span>06 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 7: Statement of the problem",
    "html": "",
    "short": "Problem"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 8: Hypermart revenue contribution",
    "html": "\n<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Company background · Revenue mix, 2020</div><h2>Hypermart is MPPA’s main chain</h2>\n<div class=\"revenue-layout\"><div><div class=\"big-share\">85%</div><p class=\"share-caption\">of revenue came from Hypermart</p></div><div class=\"revenue-rest\"><p><strong>10%</strong><br>Foodmart &amp; Primo</p><p><strong>5%</strong><br>Other formats</p><p class=\"share-caption\">Revenue contribution does not establish profitability.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Source: Case 23, Exhibit 5, printed p. 590 · Approximate shares</span><span>08 / 30</span></div>",
    "short": "Revenue mix"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 9: Store network & outlet performance",
    "short": "Outlet performance",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Company background · Retail portfolio performance</div>\n<h2>Store network changes &amp; 2020 outlet performance</h2>\n<p class=\"competitor-intro-scope\">Exhibit 6: 2018–2020 outlet counts, format sales breakdown, and decoding store openings vs closures.</p>\n<div class=\"exhibit6-layout\">\n  <div class=\"exhibit6-table-wrap\">\n    <table class=\"exhibit6-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th class=\"th-format\">Retail Format</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">2018</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">2019</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">2020</th>\n          <th class=\"th-badge-col\">2020 Stores<br>Opened / Closed</th>\n          <th class=\"th-sales\">2020 Sales<br>(Rp Billion)</th>\n          <th class=\"th-share\">Sales<br>Share</th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr class=\"tr-hypermart\">\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>Hypermart</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Flagship Hypermarket</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">117</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">102</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>100</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-prune\" title=\"0 opened, 2 closed\">0 / 2</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\"><strong>Rp 5,698</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-share highlight-share\"><strong>84.5%</strong></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>Foodmart Supermarket</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Mid-tier Supermarket</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">19</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">17</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>16</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-prune\" title=\"0 opened, 1 closed\">0 / 1</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 344</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share\">5.1%</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>Primo Supermarket</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Premium Supermarket</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">5</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">9</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>9</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-neutral\" title=\"0 opened, 0 closed\">0 / 0</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 345</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share\">5.1%</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr class=\"tr-hyfresh\">\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>Hyfresh Supermarket</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag tag-grow\">Compact Fresh Market</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">0</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">8</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>9</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-growth\" title=\"2 opened, 1 closed (+1 net)\">2 / 1</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 135</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share\">2.0%</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>Boston Health &amp; Beauty</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Pharmacy &amp; HBC Kiosk</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">74</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">69</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>62</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-heavy-prune\" title=\"0 opened, 7 closed (-7 net)\">0 / 7</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 45</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share drag-share\">0.7%</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>FMX</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Convenience Store</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">12</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">16</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>14</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-prune\" title=\"0 opened, 2 closed\">0 / 2</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 46</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share drag-share\">0.7%</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"td-format\">\n            <strong>SmartClub</strong>\n            <span class=\"format-tag\">Wholesale Club</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-neutral\" title=\"0 opened, 0 closed\">0 / 0</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\">Rp 134</td>\n          <td class=\"td-share\">2.0%</td>\n        </tr>\n      </tbody>\n      <tfoot>\n        <tr class=\"tr-totals\">\n          <td class=\"td-format\"><strong>Total Retail Network</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>219</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>222</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-num\"><strong>211</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-badge-cell\">\n            <span class=\"badge-ratio ratio-total\" title=\"2 opened, 13 closed (net -11)\">2 / 13</span>\n          </td>\n          <td class=\"td-sales\"><strong>Rp 6,747</strong></td>\n          <td class=\"td-share\"><strong>100.0%</strong></td>\n        </tr>\n      </tfoot>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"exhibit6-source-note\">\n      <span>*Case Exhibit 6 lists SmartClub at 2 stores in 2020; MPPA Annual Report 2020 notes 1 operational store. Total sales match reported net revenue of Rp6,747B.</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"exhibit6-side-panel exhibit6-visual-summary\">\n  <article class=\"ex6-visual-card\"><div><span class=\"ex6-eyebrow\">2020 network movement</span><h3>2 openings · 13 closures</h3></div><div class=\"ex6-movement\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two stores opened and 13 stores closed, net decrease of 11 stores\"><div><span>Opened</span><div class=\"ex6-track\"><i class=\"ex6-open\" style=\"width:15.4%\"></i></div><strong>2</strong></div><div><span>Closed</span><div class=\"ex6-track\"><i class=\"ex6-closed\" style=\"width:100%\"></i></div><strong>13</strong></div></div><p class=\"ex6-net\"><strong>−11</strong> net stores · 222 → 211</p></article>\n  <article class=\"ex6-visual-card\"><div><span class=\"ex6-eyebrow\">2020 sales concentration</span><h3>Hypermart is the main sales driver</h3></div><div class=\"ex6-donut-row\"><div class=\"ex6-donut\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hypermart generated 84.5 percent of sales; other formats 15.5 percent\"><span>84.5%<small>Hypermart</small></span></div><div class=\"ex6-legend\"><p><i class=\"ex6-red\"></i><b>84.5%</b> Hypermart<br><span>Rp5,698bn</span></p><p><i class=\"ex6-gray\"></i><b>15.5%</b> Other formats</p></div></div></article>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Case 23 Exhibit 6, p. 592; MPPA Annual Report 2020 pp. 3, 36, 45–48</span><span>09 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 10: Staple food market demand",
    "short": "Food demand",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Market baseline · Retail demand &amp; category scale · 2020</div>\n<h2>Market footprint: Staple food demand in 2020</h2>\n<p class=\"competitor-intro-scope\">Factual baseline of staple food consumption in Indonesia across modern and general trade (Case Exhibit 7).</p>\n<div class=\"market-stacked-layout\">\n  <div class=\"market-top-visual\">\n    <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:.25cqw;\">\n      <h3 style=\"margin:0;\">EXHIBIT 7 · Food Sales in Indonesia (2020)</h3>\n      <span style=\"font-size:.78cqw;color:#73616c;\">By type of food in millions of USD · Source: Euromonitor, 2020 (Case 23, p. 593)</span>\n    </div>\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 205\" class=\"exhibit7-chart\"  role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Exhibit 7: Food Sales in Indonesia in 2020 by Type of Food in millions of USD\">\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"15\" stroke=\"#e9dfe5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"19\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">10,000</text>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"45\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#e9dfe5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"49\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">8,000</text>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"75\" stroke=\"#e9dfe5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">6,000</text>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"105\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"105\" stroke=\"#e9dfe5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"109\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">4,000</text>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#e9dfe5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">2,000</text>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"165\" x2=\"880\" y2=\"165\" stroke=\"#30252b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <text x=\"50\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#73616c\">0</text>\n      <!-- Rice: 8,587 -->\n      <rect x=\"104\" y=\"36\" width=\"32\" height=\"129\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"120\" y=\"29\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">8,587</text>\n      <text x=\"120\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Rice</text>\n      <!-- Soft Drinks: 7,477 -->\n      <rect x=\"244\" y=\"53\" width=\"32\" height=\"112\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"260\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">7,477</text>\n      <text x=\"260\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Soft Drinks</text>\n      <!-- Dairy: 4,244 -->\n      <rect x=\"384\" y=\"101\" width=\"32\" height=\"64\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"400\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">4,244</text>\n      <text x=\"400\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Dairy</text>\n      <!-- Cooking Ingredients: 4,142 -->\n      <rect x=\"524\" y=\"103\" width=\"32\" height=\"62\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"540\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">4,142</text>\n      <text x=\"540\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Cooking Ingredients</text>\n      <!-- Noodles: 3,152 -->\n      <rect x=\"664\" y=\"118\" width=\"32\" height=\"47\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"680\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">3,152</text>\n      <text x=\"680\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Noodles</text>\n      <!-- Baby Food: 3,066 -->\n      <rect x=\"804\" y=\"119\" width=\"32\" height=\"46\" fill=\"#df0036\" rx=\"2\"/>\n      <text x=\"820\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">3,066</text>\n      <text x=\"820\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#30252b\">Baby Food</text>\n    </svg>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"market-bottom-cards\">\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>$30.7B Total Tracked Scale</h4>\n      <p>The six tracked staple categories generated <strong>$30,668 million USD</strong> in 2020 turnover. Unlike discretionary items, essential food products sustained massive, non-cyclical consumer demand.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>Rice &amp; Beverages Anchor &gt;52%</h4>\n      <p>Rice (<strong>$8,587M</strong>) and Soft Drinks (<strong>$7,477M</strong>) together account for <strong>52.4%</strong> of total staple food spending, demonstrating that basic carbohydrate staples and daily packaged beverages drive the largest monetary volume.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>Surging Digital Demand (+54% GMV)</h4>\n      <p>Indonesian e-commerce GMV expanded <strong>+54% YoY to $32B in 2020</strong> (Google, Temasek, Bain), with <em>groceries and daily essentials emerging as the fastest-surging category</em> as households avoided physical crowds.</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Case 23 Exhibit 7, printed p. 593 (Euromonitor); Google, Temasek, Bain e-Conomy SEA 2020</span><span>10 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 11: Transaction frequency & foot traffic",
    "short": "Purchase cycles",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Market baseline · Consumer purchase cycles · 2020</div>\n<h2>Market footprint: Transaction frequency &amp; foot traffic</h2>\n<p class=\"competitor-intro-scope\">Essential groceries dictate retail store visit frequency; non-food merchandise depends on food traffic.</p>\n<div class=\"market-stacked-layout\">\n  <div class=\"market-top-visual\">\n    <div class=\"market-redesign-grid\"><div><h3>Annual purchase frequency</h3><p class=\"sub\">Estimated household shopping trips per year</p><div class=\"frequency-list\"><div><span>Fresh food &amp; perishables</span><strong>100–200 <small>trips / year</small></strong></div><div><span>Packaged groceries &amp; household goods</span><strong>24–52 <small>trips / year</small></strong></div><div><span>Discretionary non-food</span><strong>1–4 <small>trips / year</small></strong></div></div></div><div><h3>Estimated store foot traffic</h3><p class=\"sub\">Illustrative midpoint of the stated ranges</p><div class=\"pie-comparison\"><div class=\"pie-graphic\" style=\"--portion:75%;--pie-color:#df0036\" aria-label=\"Illustrative midpoint: food and perishables 75%, non-food and browse 25%\"></div><div class=\"pie-legend\"><p><i></i><strong>70–80%</strong><br>Food &amp; perishables</p><p><i class=\"other\"></i><strong>20–30%</strong><br>Non-food &amp; browsing</p></div></div><p class=\"pie-note\">Pie illustrates the midpoint, not a measured point estimate.</p></div></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"market-bottom-cards\">\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>1. 2–4x Weekly Grocery Cycles</h4>\n      <p>Households buy fresh produce, meat, dairy, and bakery items <strong>2 to 4 times a week</strong> due to perishability, whereas appliances, kitchenware, or furniture are replaced once every few months or years.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>2. Groceries Drive 70–80% Foot-Traffic</h4>\n      <p>Perishables and packaged grocery items generate <strong>over 70–80% of store foot-traffic</strong> in modern hypermarkets. Fresh food acts as the primary magnet pulling consumers across the lease line.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>3. Automatic Non-Food Collapse</h4>\n      <p>Hypermarkets historically relied on weekly food trips to produce spillover browsing into higher-margin non-food aisles. When shoppers stop visiting for groceries, <em>sales for non-food items collapse automatically</em>.</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Nielsen Indonesia Shopper Trends 2020; Retail frequency benchmarks; Case 23 pp. 589–593</span><span>11 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 12: Channel migration & fresh resilience",
    "short": "Channel shift",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Market baseline · Category channel shift · 2020</div>\n<h2>Market footprint: Channel migration &amp; fresh resilience</h2>\n<p class=\"competitor-intro-scope\">Discretionary non-food permanently migrated to e-commerce, while fresh food proved resilient.</p>\n<div class=\"market-stacked-layout\">\n  <div class=\"market-top-visual\">\n    <div class=\"market-redesign-grid\"><div><h3>Channel exposure</h3><p class=\"sub\">Qualitative assessment · 2020</p><div class=\"exposure-list\"><div><strong>Non-food</strong><span>Higher exposure to online competition</span></div><div><strong>Fresh food</strong><span>Cold-chain and freshness shape delivery</span></div></div></div><div><h3>Fresh food share of MPPA sales</h3><p class=\"sub\">MPPA Annual Report 2020 · p. 38</p><div class=\"paired-pies\"><div><div class=\"pie-graphic\" style=\"--portion:24%;--pie-color:#df0036\" aria-label=\"2019: fresh food 24 percent of sales\"></div><strong>24.0%</strong><span>2019</span></div><div><div class=\"pie-graphic\" style=\"--portion:27.7%;--pie-color:#df0036\" aria-label=\"2020: fresh food 27.7 percent of sales\"></div><strong>27.7%</strong><span>2020</span></div></div><p class=\"pie-note\"><span class=\"fresh-legend\"><span><i class=\"fresh-key\"></i>Fresh food sales</span><span><i class=\"other-key\"></i>Other sales</span></span> +3.7 percentage points</p></div></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"market-bottom-cards\">\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>1. The E-Commerce Shift for General Non-Food</h4>\n      <p>By 2020, general non-food merchandise was heavily disrupted by e-commerce platforms (<strong>Shopee, Tokopedia</strong>) and specialized department stores (including sister entity <em>LPPF</em>), eroding store margins on ambient non-food.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>2. Cold-Chain Logistics Shielded Fresh Perishables</h4>\n      <p>Fresh vegetables, fruit, poultry, and meat remained insulated from ambient e-commerce disruption due to cold-chain infrastructure requirements and consumer insistence on inspecting physical freshness.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>3. Strategic Pivot: Fresh Share Surged &amp; Hyfresh Launched</h4>\n      <p>MPPA’s fresh food sales share surged to <em>27.7% in 2020</em> (AR2020 p. 38). To capture neighborhood demand in the New Normal, MPPA prioritized its compact <strong>Hyfresh</strong> supermarket format, focusing on fresh food and daily groceries while eliminating hypermarket non-food overhead (AR2020 pp. 46–47).</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: MPPA Annual Report 2020 pp. 38, 47; Google-Temasek-Bain e-Conomy SEA 2020; Case 23 pp. 590–592</span><span>12 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 13: Format substitution & proximity shift",
    "short": "Format shift",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Market baseline · Retail format dynamics · 2020</div>\n<h2>Market footprint: Format substitution in household budgets</h2>\n<p class=\"competitor-intro-scope\">Mobility curbs redirected grocery trips from mall hypermarkets to neighborhood minimarkets.</p>\n<div class=\"market-stacked-layout\">\n  <div class=\"market-top-visual\">\n    <div class=\"market-top-grid\">\n      <div>\n        <h3>Modern Food Retail Store Count in Indonesia (2020)</h3>\n        <p class=\"sub\">Total operational outlets by format · Sources: Company Annual Reports 2020</p>\n        <div class=\"market-meter-group\">\n          <div class=\"market-meter-row\">\n            <span>Indomaret (Minimarket)</span>\n            <div class=\"market-meter-track\"><div class=\"market-meter-fill brand-fill\" style=\"width:100%\"></div></div>\n            <b>18,113 stores</b>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"market-meter-row\">\n            <span>Alfamart (Minimarket)</span>\n            <div class=\"market-meter-track\"><div class=\"market-meter-fill brand-fill\" style=\"width:85.2%\"></div></div>\n            <b>15,434 stores</b>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"market-meter-row\">\n            <span>Alfamidi (Supermarket)</span>\n            <div class=\"market-meter-track\"><div class=\"market-meter-fill dark-fill\" style=\"width:10%\"></div></div>\n            <b>1,821 stores</b>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"market-meter-row\">\n            <span>Hypermart / MPPA</span>\n            <div class=\"market-meter-track\"><div class=\"market-meter-fill\" style=\"width:1.2%\"></div></div>\n            <b>100 hyper (219 tot)</b>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <div class=\"traffic-split-wrap\">\n          <div class=\"traffic-stat-box\">\n            <strong>94%+</strong>\n            <span>Modern Store Network Held by Minimarkets</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"traffic-divider\"></div>\n          <div class=\"traffic-stat-box\">\n            <strong>&lt;1%</strong>\n            <span>Hypermarkets Share of Total Outlets</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:.76cqw;color:#73616c;margin:.35cqw 0 0;text-align:center;\">Over 33,500 neighborhood stores captured daily grocery runs during PSBB curbs.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"market-bottom-cards\">\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>1. Inelastic Sustenance Spending Persisted</h4>\n      <p>During COVID-19 mobility curbs, consumers did not stop eating or reduce staple food intake; household grocery budgets remained active and non-negotiable throughout 2020.</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>2. Proximity Trumps Destination Mall Shopping</h4>\n      <p>Shoppers redirected weekly trips away from large mall-anchored hypermarkets (Hypermart, Transmart) toward nearby neighborhood minimarkets (<strong>Indomaret, Alfamart</strong>) and fresh residential supermarkets (<strong>Alfamidi</strong>).</p>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"market-fact-card\">\n      <h4>3. Structural Redistribution of Food Retail Revenue</h4>\n      <p>With over <em>33,500 combined minimarkets</em> positioned within residential clusters, neighborhood formats captured the grocery spend previously captured by mall hypermarkets, compounding Hypermart's revenue contraction.</p>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Case 23 Exhibit 8; Indoritel AR2020; Sumber Alfaria AR2020; Alfamidi AR2020</span><span>13 / 30</span></div>"
  },
