0.10</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"efe-row\" data-code=\"T7\" data-type=\"Threat\" data-name=\"Heavy Fixed Long-Term Lease Obligations\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Poor\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.04\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 54–55 · Slide 14 & 15\" data-rationale=\"Poor response (Rating 1): Rigid lease structures create heavy right-of-use asset depreciation and financing charges regardless of store sales.\" data-hover-reason=\"MPPA still faced long-term lease costs even when store sales fell, leaving little room to adjust occupancy costs.\" data-weight-reason=\"Fixed leases amplify cash pressure when sales fall.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"efe-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"efe-code\">T7</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-name\">Heavy Fixed Long-Term Lease Obligations</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-metric\">Rp166B net finance cost</span>\n            <div class=\"efe-tooltip\">\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-top\">\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-badge efe-badge-threat\">Threat T7 · R1</span>\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-src\">AR2020 pp. 54–55 · Slide 14 & 15</span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-text\"><strong>Analytical Rationale:</strong> Poor response (Rating 1): Rigid lease structures create heavy right-of-use asset depreciation and financing charges regardless of store sales.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.04</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"efe-row\" data-code=\"T8\" data-type=\"Threat\" data-name=\"Zero Brand Switching Costs for Grocery Shoppers\" data-rating=\"2\" data-rating-label=\"Average\" data-weight=\"0.03\" data-ws=\"0.06\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 8; Nielsen 2020 · Slide 16\" data-rationale=\"Average response (Rating 2): Price match guarantees protect staple price perception but trigger ongoing retail gross margin compression.\" data-hover-reason=\"MPPA used price matching to keep staples competitive, but that response put pressure on margins.\" data-weight-reason=\"Customers can switch stores easily when prices differ.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"efe-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"efe-code\">T8</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-name\">Zero Brand Switching Costs for Grocery Shoppers</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-metric\">Promotion-driven splitting</span>\n            <div class=\"efe-tooltip\">\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-top\">\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-badge efe-badge-threat\">Threat T8 · R2</span>\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-src\">Case Exhibit 8; Nielsen 2020 · Slide 16</span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-text\"><strong>Analytical Rationale:</strong> Average response (Rating 2): Price match guarantees protect staple price perception but trigger ongoing retail gross margin compression.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.03</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">2</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.06</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"efe-row\" data-code=\"T9\" data-type=\"Threat\" data-name=\"Delivery App Commission Fees\" data-rating=\"2\" data-rating-label=\"Average\" data-weight=\"0.03\" data-ws=\"0.06\" data-source=\"Industry benchmarks · Slide 15 & 16\" data-rationale=\"Average response (Rating 2): Rapid partner onboarding generated sales volume but aggregator commissions erode already slim grocery margins.\" data-hover-reason=\"Delivery partners brought in orders, but their commissions reduced the margin on those sales.\" data-weight-reason=\"Commission costs determine how profitable online orders are.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"efe-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"efe-code\">T9</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-name\">Delivery App Commission Fees</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-metric\">5%–15% delivery cuts</span>\n            <div class=\"efe-tooltip\">\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-top\">\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-badge efe-badge-threat\">Threat T9 · R2</span>\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-src\">Industry benchmarks · Slide 15 & 16</span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-text\"><strong>Analytical Rationale:</strong> Average response (Rating 2): Rapid partner onboarding generated sales volume but aggregator commissions erode already slim grocery margins.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.03</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">2</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.06</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"efe-row\" data-code=\"T10\" data-type=\"Threat\" data-name=\"Deep Cash Reserves of Rival Conglomerates\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Poor\" data-weight=\"0.03\" data-ws=\"0.03\" data-source=\"Competitor AR2020 · Slide 18 & 19\" data-rationale=\"Poor response (Rating 1): MPPA’s negative operating cash flow (−Rp80B) prevents aggressive price subsidy wars against deep-pocketed peers.\" data-hover-reason=\"With roughly Rp80 billion in negative operating cash flow, MPPA had little capacity to match well-funded rivals in a price war.\" data-weight-reason=\"Cash reserves determine how long retailers can fund discounts.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"efe-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"efe-code\">T10</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-name\">Deep Cash Reserves of Rival Conglomerates</span>\n            <span class=\"efe-metric\">Salim / Alfaria cash reserves</span>\n            <div class=\"efe-tooltip\">\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-top\">\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-badge efe-badge-threat\">Threat T10 · R1</span>\n                <span class=\"efe-tt-src\">Competitor AR2020 · Slide 18 & 19</span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"efe-tt-text\"><strong>Analytical Rationale:</strong> Poor response (Rating 1): MPPA’s negative operating cash flow (−Rp80B) prevents aggressive price subsidy wars against deep-pocketed peers.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.03</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.03</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"efe-subtotal\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\"><strong>Threats Subtotal</strong></td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.50</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">—</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.79</td>\n      </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"efe-footer-bar\">\n  <span><strong>Ratings (R):</strong> 1 = Poor Response · 2 = Average · 3 = Above Average · 4 = Superior Response</span>\n  <span><strong>EFE Total Score:</strong> Weight <strong>1.00</strong> · Weighted Score <span class=\"efe-total-pill\">2.46</span> (Industry Threshold: 2.50)</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\">\n  <span>Sources: Google-Temasek-Bain; BI / BPS; Nielsen; Case 23; AR2020 (MPPA, AMRT, MIDI, Indoritel)</span>\n  <span>20 / 30</span>\n</div>"
