    "label": "Slide 21: Internal Factor Evaluation (IFE Matrix)",
    "short": "IFE Matrix",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Strategy formulation · Stage 1 · Input</div>\n<h2>Internal Factor Evaluation (IFE Matrix)</h2>\n<div class=\"ife-inspector\" id=\"ife-ins-box\">\n  <div class=\"ife-ins-head\">\n    <span class=\"ife-ins-pill ife-pill-str\" id=\"ife-ins-pill\">Strength S1</span>\n    <span class=\"ife-ins-title\" id=\"ife-ins-title\">Fresh Food Revenue Contribution Expansion · Rating 4 (Major Strength) · W: 0.07 (WS: 0.28)</span>\n    <span class=\"ife-ins-source\" id=\"ife-ins-source\">AR2020 p. 38 · Slide 12</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ife-ins-body\" id=\"ife-ins-body\">\n    <strong>Analytical Rationale:</strong> Fresh food is MPPA’s primary traffic driver and highest-frequency department, successfully insulating top-line revenue during pandemic mobility restrictions.\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ife-matrix-wrap\">\n  <div class=\"ife-column\">\n    <div class=\"ife-col-head\">\n      <span class=\"ife-col-title\">10 Strengths</span>\n      <span class=\"ife-col-badge\">Subtotal: 0.45 | 1.53</span>\n    </div>\n    <table class=\"ife-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th class=\"th-factor\">Critical Internal Factor</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">W</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">R</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">WS</th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S1\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Fresh food share of sales\" data-rating=\"4\" data-rating-label=\"Major Strength\" data-weight=\"0.07\" data-ws=\"0.28\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 38 · Slide 12\" data-rationale=\"Fresh food is MPPA’s primary traffic driver and highest-frequency department, successfully insulating top-line revenue during pandemic mobility restrictions.\" data-hover-reason=\"Fresh food drew repeat visits and rose from 24.0% to 27.7% of sales in 2020, making it a core strength for MPPA.\" data-weight-reason=\"Fresh food drives repeat visits and a large share of revenue.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S1</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Fresh food share of sales</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">27.7% of sales (+3.7% YoY)</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.07</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">4</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.28</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S2\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Central Cold-Chain Distribution Centers\" data-rating=\"4\" data-rating-label=\"Major Strength\" data-weight=\"0.06\" data-ws=\"0.24\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 38, 126 · Slide 12 & 17\" data-rationale=\"Temperature-controlled multi-facility logistics network forms a high capital-barrier moat that ambient parcel-delivery e-commerce cannot replicate.\" data-hover-reason=\"Three temperature-controlled distribution centers helped MPPA supply fresh products reliably across its network.\" data-weight-reason=\"Cold-chain reliability is central to the fresh-food offer.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S2</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Central Cold-Chain Distribution Centers</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">3 DCs, 66,755 m² capacity</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.06</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">4</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.24</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S3\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"National Hypermarket Store Network\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.05\" data-ws=\"0.15\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 6, p. 592 · Slide 8 & 9\" data-rationale=\"High brand visibility and irreplaceable prime real estate anchors across outer island provincial hubs spanning Sumatra to Papua.\" data-hover-reason=\"A network of 100 hypermarkets gave MPPA national visibility and established locations, although the large format was less convenient for quick trips.\" data-weight-reason=\"Store locations influence access and market reach.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S3</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">National Hypermarket Store Network</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">100 stores across 73 cities</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.05</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.15</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S4\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Fast Multi-Platform Online Delivery\" data-rating=\"4\" data-rating-label=\"Major Strength\" data-weight=\"0.05\" data-ws=\"0.20\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 25 · Slide 15\" data-rationale=\"Fast asset-light rollout converted physical hypermarkets into localized e-grocery fulfillment nodes without fleet capital expenditure.\" data-hover-reason=\"MPPA rolled out online ordering quickly and used existing stores to fill orders without buying its own delivery fleet.\" data-weight-reason=\"Online fulfillment helped keep stores productive during mobility restrictions.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S4</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Fast Multi-Platform Online Delivery</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">103 online, 97 GrabMart stores</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.05</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">4</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.20</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S5\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Direct FMCG Supplier Distribution\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.12\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 12, 126 · Slide 16 & 17\" data-rationale=\"Direct relationships with multinational FMCG manufacturers ensure consolidated bulk supply and vendor promotional support during transit disruptions.\" data-hover-reason=\"Direct supplier relationships supported bulk purchasing and promotions, while MPPA still competed against larger minimarket networks.\" data-weight-reason=\"Supplier terms affect availability and purchase costs.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S5</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Direct FMCG Supplier Distribution</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">750+ vendors, 53.8% DC flow</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.12</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S6\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"National Halal Logistics Certification\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.12\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 25, 41\" data-rationale=\"Full compliance with national Halal supply chain integrity provides strong institutional trust among Indonesia’s 87% Muslim consumer majority.\" data-hover-reason=\"Halal certification across all three central distribution centers helped build trust in how MPPA handled products.\" data-weight-reason=\"Halal handling matters to customers who rely on that assurance.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S6</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">National Halal Logistics Certification</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">First Halal DC certification</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.12</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S7\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Compact Fresh Supermarket Formats\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.12\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 4; AR2020 pp. 46–47 · Slide 12\" data-rationale=\"Smaller 500–1,500 m² formats offer a proven operational template to expand into high-frequency residential neighborhoods without hypermarket drag.\" data-hover-reason=\"Foodmart and the first two Hyfresh stores gave MPPA a smaller format it could use in neighborhoods, though Hyfresh was still a pilot.\" data-weight-reason=\"Smaller formats can reach shoppers underserved by large stores.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S7</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Compact Fresh Supermarket Formats</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">23 Foodmart, 2 Hyfresh stores</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.12</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S8\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Private Label In-House Brands\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.12\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 45\" data-rationale=\"In-house staple brands provide budget-conscious shoppers 15–20% lower price points while yielding MPPA 300–500 bps higher gross margins.\" data-hover-reason=\"MPPA’s own brands offered lower-priced staples and could earn better margins than branded alternatives.\" data-weight-reason=\"Private labels help balance affordability and margin.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S8</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Private Label In-House Brands</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">1,200+ Value Plus / Hypermart SKUs</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.12</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S9\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"100% Focus on Direct Retail Shoppers\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.03\" data-ws=\"0.09\" data-source=\"Case p. 587; AR2020 p. 38 · Slide 2\" data-rationale=\"Exiting thin-margin B2B wholesale distribution eliminated operational distractions and protected core grocery gross margins at 16.7%.\" data-hover-reason=\"Focusing on direct retail let MPPA concentrate on grocery shoppers after leaving thin-margin wholesale.\" data-weight-reason=\"Management focus affects where limited resources go.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S9</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">100% Focus on Direct Retail Shoppers</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">100% direct retail focus</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.03</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.09</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"S10\" data-type=\"Strength\" data-name=\"Large Registered Loyalty Customer Base\" data-rating=\"3\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Strength\" data-weight=\"0.03\" data-ws=\"0.09\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 4; AR2020 p. 43\" data-rationale=\"Established membership base provides direct digital reach and purchase history data to drive repeat grocery transaction cycles.\" data-hover-reason=\"The established Hicard membership gave MPPA a way to reach repeat customers and understand their buying habits.\" data-weight-reason=\"Loyalty data supports retention and targeted offers.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">S10</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Large Registered Loyalty Customer Base</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">~3.5M Hicard registered members</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.03</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">3</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.09</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-subtotal\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\"><strong>Strengths Subtotal</strong></td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.45</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">—</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">1.53</td>\n      </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ife-column\">\n    <div class=\"ife-col-head\">\n      <span class=\"ife-col-title\">10 Weaknesses</span>\n      <span class=\"ife-col-badge\">Subtotal: 0.55 | 0.68</span>\n    </div>\n    <table class=\"ife-table\">\n      <thead>\n        <tr>\n          <th class=\"th-factor\">Critical Internal Factor</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">W</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">R</th>\n          <th class=\"th-num\">WS</th>\n        </tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W1\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Four Straight Years of Heavy Net Losses\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.08\" data-ws=\"0.08\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 53; Case Exhibit 5 · Slide 9\" data-rationale=\"Chronic losses depleted equity down to Rp460.6B by end-2020, severely threatening financial going-concern status and limiting capital investments.\" data-hover-reason=\"Four years of losses eroded equity and left MPPA with much less room to invest in a recovery.\" data-weight-reason=\"Persistent losses threaten the ability to fund the business.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W1</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Four Straight Years of Heavy Net Losses</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">−Rp887.5B in 2020 (−Rp3.53T cumulative)</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.08</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.08</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W2\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Negative Cash Flow from Store Operations\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.07\" data-ws=\"0.07\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 56 · Slide 18\" data-rationale=\"Operating activities fail to self-fund working capital or required store maintenance capex, forcing reliance on bank debt and supplier credit stretching.\" data-hover-reason=\"Operations used cash in 2020 instead of generating it, leaving MPPA reliant on external funding or supplier credit.\" data-weight-reason=\"Operating cash pays for inventory and day-to-day expenses.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W2</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Negative Cash Flow from Store Operations</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">−Rp80.4B operating cash outflow</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.07</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.07</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W3\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Over-Reliance on Big Hypermarket Stores\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.06\" data-ws=\"0.06\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 5; AR2020 p. 38 · Slide 8 & 9\" data-rationale=\"Extreme structural concentration in massive 5,000–8,000 m² stores leaves MPPA heavily exposed to consumer migration toward neighborhood minimarkets.\" data-hover-reason=\"Hypermart generated 84.5% of sales, so the shift toward smaller neighborhood stores exposed most of MPPA’s revenue.\" data-weight-reason=\"Concentration makes a single format’s decline a company-wide risk.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W3</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Over-Reliance on Big Hypermarket Stores</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">Hypermart drives 84.5% of sales</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.06</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.06</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W4\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Vulnerability to Shopping Mall Foot-Traffic Drops\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.06\" data-ws=\"0.06\" data-source=\"Case p. 587; AR2020 p. 38 · Slide 11 & 14\" data-rationale=\"Shopping mall operating curfews and 50% capacity caps decimated weekend family foot-traffic, causing fixed occupancy overhead to overwhelm sales.\" data-hover-reason=\"Many stores relied on mall visitors, so restrictions reduced traffic while store costs continued.\" data-weight-reason=\"Store traffic affects sales while occupancy costs remain due.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W4</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Vulnerability to Shopping Mall Foot-Traffic Drops</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">Over 80% stores anchored in malls</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.06</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.06</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W5\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Heavy PSAK 73 Lease and Interest Overhead\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.06\" data-ws=\"0.06\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 54–55 · Slide 14\" data-rationale=\"Rigid long-term hypermarket lease liabilities (Rp2.25T) produce massive right-of-use asset depreciation and finance costs regardless of sales.\" data-hover-reason=\"Long-term leases and their financing costs remained due even when sales weakened.\" data-weight-reason=\"Committed lease costs limit the cash available for recovery.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W5</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Heavy PSAK 73 Lease and Interest Overhead</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">Rp166.2B net finance cost (14.8% GP)</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.06</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.06</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W6\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Low Sales per Square Meter of Floor Space\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.05\" data-ws=\"0.05\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 12; Competitor ARs · Slide 13 & 18\" data-rationale=\"Vast non-food hypermarket floor space sits unproductive as discretionary goods migrate online, dragging total space efficiency to less than half of peers.\" data-hover-reason=\"MPPA generated about Rp8.9 million per square meter versus Alfamidi’s Rp18.2 million, leaving its larger space less productive.\" data-weight-reason=\"Sales per square meter show whether stores earn enough from their space.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W6</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Low Sales per Square Meter of Floor Space</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">Rp8.9M/m² (vs. Alfamidi Rp18.2M/m²)</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.05</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.05</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W7\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Too Many Fragmented Small Store Brands\" data-rating=\"2\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.05\" data-ws=\"0.10\" data-source=\"Case Exhibit 4; AR2020 p. 46 · Slide 3\" data-rationale=\"Operating Foodmart, Primo, Hyfresh, and FMX simultaneously fragments marketing resources and confuses consumers, lacking a unified umbrella identity.\" data-hover-reason=\"Foodmart, Primo, Hyfresh and FMX split marketing effort across four banners, making it harder to build a clear small-store identity.\" data-weight-reason=\"Fragmented brands make expansion and marketing less efficient.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W7</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Too Many Fragmented Small Store Brands</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">36 total small stores across 4 brands</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.05</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">2</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.10</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W8\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"Working capital shortfall\" data-rating=\"1\" data-rating-label=\"Major Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.04\" data-source=\"AR2020 · Consolidated statement of financial position\" data-rationale=\"Current liabilities exceeded current assets by about Rp1.23 trillion at year-end 2020.\" data-hover-reason=\"At year-end 2020, short-term liabilities exceeded short-term assets by about Rp1.23 trillion, creating immediate liquidity pressure.\" data-weight-reason=\"The shortfall affects the ability to pay near-term bills.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W8</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">Working capital shortfall</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">Rp1.23 trillion shortfall</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">1</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.04</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W9\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"High Fixed Store Operating Costs\" data-rating=\"2\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.08\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 53 · Slide 9\" data-rationale=\"Large store electricity, air conditioning, and store staffing costs cannot be reduced proportionally to top-line revenue contractions.\" data-hover-reason=\"Staffing, electricity and air conditioning could not fall as quickly as sales in large stores.\" data-weight-reason=\"Fixed costs make profits more sensitive to sales declines.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W9</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">High Fixed Store Operating Costs</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">OPEX consumed 18.2% of net sales</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">2</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.08</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-row\" data-code=\"W10\" data-type=\"Weakness\" data-name=\"No Dedicated High-Engagement Mobile App\" data-rating=\"2\" data-rating-label=\"Minor Weakness\" data-weight=\"0.04\" data-ws=\"0.08\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 25 vs. AMRT AR2020 p. 32 · Slide 18 & 19\" data-rationale=\"Ceding customer ordering to third-party aggregators (Grab, Shopee) surrenders valuable repeat customer purchase data and incurs margin commissions.\" data-hover-reason=\"Third-party apps helped MPPA sell online, but limited its access to customer data and charged commissions.\" data-weight-reason=\"Direct customer data and commission costs matter for profitable repeat orders.\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\">\n          <div class=\"ife-factor-wrap\">\n            <span class=\"ife-code\">W10</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-name\">No Dedicated High-Engagement Mobile App</span>\n            <span class=\"ife-metric\">No super-app (vs. Alfagift over 8M downloads)</span>\n          </div>\n        </td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.04</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">2</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.08</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr class=\"ife-subtotal\">\n        <td class=\"td-factor\"><strong>Weaknesses Subtotal</strong></td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">0.55</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num\">—</td>\n        <td class=\"td-num td-score\">0.68</td>\n      </tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ife-footer-bar\">\n  <span><strong>Ratings (R):</strong> 1 = Major Weakness · 2 = Minor Weakness · 3 = Minor Strength · 4 = Major Strength</span>\n  <span><strong>IFE Total Score:</strong> Weight <strong>1.00</strong> · Weighted Score <span class=\"ife-total-pill\">2.21</span> (Industry Threshold: 2.50)</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\">\n  <span>Sources: MPPA Annual Report 2020; Case 23 Exhibit 4, 5, 6; Competitor AR2020 Disclosures</span>\n  <span>21 / 30</span>\n</div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 22: SWOT Matrix (TOWS)",
    "short": "SWOT Matrix",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Strategy formulation · Stage 2 · Matching</div>\n<h2>SWOT Matrix (TOWS)</h2>\n<div class=\"tows-inspector\" id=\"tows-ins-box\">\n  <div class=\"tows-ins-head\">\n    <span class=\"tows-ins-pill tows-pill-so\" id=\"tows-ins-pill\">SO 1 (MAXI-MAXI)</span>\n    <span class=\"tows-ins-title\" id=\"tows-ins-title\">Partner with GrabMart, Shopee &amp; HappyFresh · Factors: S2, S7, O1, O8</span>\n    <div class=\"brand-pill-wrap\" id=\"tows-ins-logos\">\n      <span class=\"brand-pill pill-hypermart\">Hypermart</span>\n      <span class=\"brand-pill pill-grab\">GrabMart</span>\n      <span class=\"brand-pill pill-ovo\">OVO</span>\n      <span class=\"brand-pill pill-shopee\">Shopee</span>\n    </div>\n    <span class=\"tows-ins-source\" id=\"tows-ins-source\">AR2020 p. 40</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"tows-ins-body\" id=\"tows-ins-body\">\n    <strong>Strategic Implementation Rationale:</strong> Instead of spending money to buy delivery vans, Hypermart partners with Grab drivers. In 2020, online sales jumped from under 0.1% to 4.5% of total sales. Because 93% of new online shoppers plan to keep buying groceries online, Hypermart uses Grab&#39;s drivers to deliver food within 30 minutes straight from existing stores.\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tows-grid\">\n    <div class=\"tows-card tows-card-so\">\n      <div class=\"tows-card-head\">\n        <span class=\"tows-card-title\">SO Strategies (Strengths · Opportunities)</span>\n        <span class=\"tows-badge tows-badge-so\">Maxi–Maxi · Growth</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tows-list\">\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"SO 1\" data-type=\"SO\" data-name=\"Partner with GrabMart, Shopee & HappyFresh for Fast Delivery\" data-tags=\"S2, S7, O1, O8\" data-logos=\"hypermart,grab,ovo,shopee\" data-desc=\"Use all 100 Hypermart stores as dispatch hubs for GrabMart, Shopee, and HappyFresh to capture the 54% boom in online grocery buying.\" data-expl=\"Instead of spending money to buy delivery vans, Hypermart partners with Grab drivers. In 2020, online sales jumped from under 0.1% to 4.5% of total sales. Because 93% of new online shoppers plan to keep buying groceries online, Hypermart uses Grab's drivers to deliver food within 30 minutes straight from existing stores.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 40, 54; Case p. 594\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s store and cold-chain network with rising online grocery demand and wider access to delivery partners.\" data-hover-reason=\"Using existing stores to fill orders lets MPPA reach more shoppers without building a separate warehouse or delivery network.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-so\">SO 1</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Partner with GrabMart, Shopee & HappyFresh for Fast Delivery</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S2, S7, O1, O8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Use all 100 Hypermart stores as dispatch hubs for GrabMart, Shopee, and HappyFresh to capture the 54% boom in online grocery buying.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"SO 2\" data-type=\"SO\" data-name=\"Buy Fresh Food Directly from Farmers via Cold Storage\" data-tags=\"S1, S4, O3, O7, O10\" data-logos=\"hypermart,dc\" data-desc=\"Use Hypermart's large chilled distribution centers (66,755 m²) to buy vegetables, fruit, and meat directly from local farmers in bulk.\" data-expl=\"Indonesia's staple food market is worth $30.7 billion. Hypermart has 2 large cold-storage warehouses in Balaraja and Surabaya where 54% of goods flow centrally. Buying directly from farmers cuts out expensive middlemen and keeps vegetables fresh, cutting down on food waste and protecting profit margins.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 12, 48; Case p. 593\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s fresh-food business and chilled distribution capacity with steady grocery demand and opportunities to source locally.\" data-hover-reason=\"Buying directly from farmers gives MPPA more control over freshness and supply, while its existing cold chain helps keep produce in good condition.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-so\">SO 2</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Buy Fresh Food Directly from Farmers via Cold Storage</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S1, S4, O3, O7, O10]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Use Hypermart's large chilled distribution centers (66,755 m²) to buy vegetables, fruit, and meat directly from local farmers in bulk.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"SO 3\" data-type=\"SO\" data-name=\"Open Small Hyfresh Neighborhood Supermarkets\" data-tags=\"S3, S6, O4, O5, O6\" data-logos=\"hyfresh\" data-desc=\"Open small, compact Hyfresh stores (500–1,000 m²) close to residential homes, taking advantage of essential food permits during COVID.\" data-expl=\"While large mall hypermarket sales fell 22%, Hyfresh was the only format that grew in 2020 (adding 1 store and reaching Rp58 billion in sales). Because supermarkets were allowed to stay open during lockdowns, building smaller stores near where people live lets shoppers buy daily fresh food without visiting crowded malls.\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 46; Case pp. 587, 592\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s retail experience with shoppers’ growing preference for nearby stores and fresh ingredients.\" data-hover-reason=\"A compact Hyfresh can serve frequent neighborhood trips with less space than a full hypermarket.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-so\">SO 3</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Open Small Hyfresh Neighborhood Supermarkets</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S3, S6, O4, O5, O6]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Open small, compact Hyfresh stores (500–1,000 m²) close to residential homes, taking advantage of essential food permits during COVID.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"SO 4\" data-type=\"SO\" data-name=\"Rebrand &amp; Unify Storefronts Under the MPPA 'Hy-' Master Brand Umbrella\" data-tags=\"S2, S8, O1, O2, O8\" data-logos=\"hypermart,hyfresh,boston\" data-desc=\"Unify fragmented small formats (Foodmart, Primo, viable kiosks) under the MPPA master brand umbrella ('Hy-') while deploying hybrid O2O on-demand fulfillment bays.\" data-expl=\"Rather than diluting marketing across obscure sub-brands (Foodmart, Primo, FMX), MPPA adopts the Alfamidi playbook: unite all grocery retail under the proprietary 'Hy-' master brand (Hypermart &amp; Hyfresh) with shared loyalty, active customer storefronts, and backroom on-demand fulfillment bays. This concentrates 100% of brand equity and marketing spend behind MPPA's core identity.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 25, 40; Case Exhibit 4 &amp; 6; MPPA Brand Architecture\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s existing retail and fulfillment capabilities with the shift to online and multichannel shopping.\" data-hover-reason=\"A shared Hy- brand can make the formats easier to recognize while letting stores serve both walk-in and online orders.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-so\">SO 4</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Rebrand &amp; Unify Storefronts Under MPPA 'Hy-' Master Brand</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S2, S8, O1, O2, O8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Unify fragmented small formats under the MPPA master brand ('Hy-') while maintaining active customer storefronts with hybrid O2O delivery bays.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tows-card tows-card-wo\">\n      <div class=\"tows-card-head\">\n        <span class=\"tows-card-title\">WO Strategies (Weaknesses · Opportunities)</span>\n        <span class=\"tows-badge tows-badge-wo\">Mini–Maxi · Turnaround</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tows-list\">\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WO 1\" data-type=\"WO\" data-name=\"Sublease 30%–40% of Big Hypermarkets to Cut Rent\" data-tags=\"W3, W6, O1, O8\" data-logos=\"hypermart,sublease\" data-desc=\"Rent out 30% to 40% of excess hypermarket retail floor space to other businesses to lower rental costs and stop lease losses.\" data-expl=\"Hypermarkets bring in 84.5% of MPPA's sales, but mall foot-traffic dropped nearly 50% during COVID. Subleasing unused floor space to pharmacies, specialty shops, or delivery hubs brings in rental income, cuts monthly electricity and staff bills, and right-sizes store space.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 38, 55; Case p. 590\" data-hover-match=\"We matched oversized, underused Hypermart space with growth in online ordering and delivery.\" data-hover-reason=\"Subleasing excess floor space helps cover rent while the retained store and backroom can serve walk-in shoppers and online orders.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wo\">WO 1</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Sublease 30%–40% of Big Hypermarkets to Cut Rent</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W3, W6, O1, O8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Rent out 30% to 40% of excess hypermarket retail floor space to other businesses to lower rental costs and stop lease losses.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WO 2\" data-type=\"WO\" data-name=\"Connect Hypermart Loyalty with OVO for Faster Cash Flow\" data-tags=\"W4, W8, O2, O3\" data-logos=\"hypermart,ovo\" data-desc=\"Link Hypermart's Hicard with OVO digital wallet points to give loyal shoppers instant rewards instead of burning money on big discounts.\" data-expl=\"MPPA takes 45 days to turn inventory into cash, and operating cash flow was negative (-Rp80 billion). Instead of spending huge money on storewide discounts, Hypermart can use OVO cashback points. This brings shoppers back weekly and brings in immediate cash without hurting gross margins.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 41, 55; Note 8\" data-hover-match=\"We matched weaker mall traffic and a working-capital shortfall with growth in digital shopping and recurring demand for essentials.\" data-hover-reason=\"Connecting Hicard with OVO gives customers a reason to return through targeted rewards. Faster cash collection would depend on the settlement terms MPPA negotiates.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wo\">WO 2</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Connect Hypermart Loyalty with OVO for Faster Cash Flow</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W4, W8, O2, O3]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Link Hypermart's Hicard with OVO digital wallet points to give loyal shoppers instant rewards instead of burning money on big discounts.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WO 3\" data-type=\"WO\" data-name=\"Contract Directly with Farmers to Stop Food Spoilage\" data-tags=\"W7, W9, O7, O9, O10\" data-logos=\"hypermart,dc\" data-desc=\"Sign supply contracts directly with local farm groups to deliver fresh produce straight to chilled warehouses, cutting rot and waste.\" data-expl=\"Fresh vegetables and fruit spoil quickly if they sit in trucks too long. Nationally, Indonesia wastes 23 to 48 million tonnes of food. By working directly with 750+ verified farm suppliers through temperature-controlled distribution centers, Hypermart gets fresher produce at lower cost with far less spoilage.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 12, 48-49\" data-hover-match=\"We matched pressure on operating costs with an opportunity to reduce spoilage through local suppliers and cold storage.\" data-hover-reason=\"Farmer contracts can shorten the route to MPPA’s warehouses and improve control over order timing and product quality.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wo\">WO 3</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Contract Directly with Farmers to Stop Food Spoilage</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W7, W9, O7, O9, O10]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Sign supply contracts directly with local farm groups to deliver fresh produce straight to chilled warehouses, cutting rot and waste.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WO 4\" data-type=\"WO\" data-name=\"Negotiate Lower Delivery Fees with Grab via High Volume\" data-tags=\"W2, W10, O1, O8\" data-logos=\"hypermart,grab,shopee\" data-desc=\"Negotiate discounted commission rates with Grab and delivery apps in exchange for being their biggest exclusive fresh food partner.\" data-expl=\"Delivery apps usually take 5% to 15% commission, which eats up grocery profits. But Grab needs Hypermart because Grab has no warehouses or meat/vegetable cold storage. By guaranteeing high order volume across 100 stores, Hypermart negotiates much lower commission fees and free app promotion.\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 40; Case p. 594\" data-hover-match=\"We matched weak operating cash flow and reliance on third-party apps with rising demand for grocery delivery.\" data-hover-reason=\"If MPPA can offer steady order volume, it has a reason to ask Grab for lower fees so online sales leave more margin.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wo\">WO 4</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Negotiate Lower Delivery Fees with Grab via High Volume</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W2, W10, O1, O8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Negotiate discounted commission rates with Grab and delivery apps in exchange for being their biggest exclusive fresh food partner.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tows-card tows-card-st\">\n      <div class=\"tows-card-head\">\n        <span class=\"tows-card-title\">ST Strategies (Strengths · Threats)</span>\n        <span class=\"tows-badge tows-badge-st\">Maxi–Mini · Defense</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tows-list\">\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"ST 1\" data-type=\"ST\" data-name=\"Sell Fresh Meat & Produce that Minimarkets Cannot Carry\" data-tags=\"S1, S4, T1, T6\" data-logos=\"hypermart,vs,indomaret,alfamart\" data-desc=\"Sell high-quality fresh beef, chicken, fish, and vegetables that small minimarkets (Indomaret and Alfamart) physically cannot keep in stock.\" data-expl=\"Indomaret and Alfamart have over 33,500 stores, but their stores are tiny (100 to 150 m²) with only dry snacks and small drink coolers. They cannot sell fresh butcher meat or bulk fresh produce. Fresh food is 27.7% of MPPA's sales, making it Hypermart's strongest shield against minimarkets.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 2, 38; Case p. 593\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s fresh-food strength with the threat from Indomaret, Alfamart and nearby fresh-food rivals such as Alfamidi.\" data-hover-reason=\"Fresh food made up 27.7% of MPPA sales. A strong meat and produce offer gives shoppers a reason to choose Hypermart even when a minimarket is closer.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-st\">ST 1</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Sell Fresh Meat & Produce that Minimarkets Cannot Carry</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S1, S4, T1, T6]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Sell high-quality fresh beef, chicken, fish, and vegetables that small minimarkets (Indomaret and Alfamart) physically cannot keep in stock.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"ST 2\" data-type=\"ST\" data-name=\"Use Hyfresh Stores to Compete Directly with Alfamidi\" data-tags=\"S3, S6, T1, T6\" data-logos=\"hyfresh,vs,alfamidi\" data-desc=\"Expand compact Hyfresh neighborhood supermarkets to prevent Alfamidi from stealing residential grocery shoppers.\" data-expl=\"Alfamidi has 1,821 mid-sized fresh supermarkets located near housing complexes, intercepting shoppers before they reach Hypermart. Hyfresh is MPPA's perfect answer: a clean, compact 500–1,000 m² neighborhood supermarket that matches Alfamidi's convenience.\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 46; MIDI AR2020; Case p. 593\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s retail experience with the threat of Alfamidi winning frequent neighborhood trips.\" data-hover-reason=\"Putting compact Hyfresh stores closer to households lets MPPA compete on convenience as well as freshness.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-st\">ST 2</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Use Hyfresh Stores to Compete Directly with Alfamidi</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S3, S6, T1, T6]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Expand compact Hyfresh neighborhood supermarkets to prevent Alfamidi from stealing residential grocery shoppers.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"ST 3\" data-type=\"ST\" data-name=\"Offer Big Family Bulk Packs on Rice and Cooking Oil\" data-tags=\"S4, S10, T2, T3, T8\" data-logos=\"hypermart,dc\" data-desc=\"Use bulk warehouse purchasing to sell large multi-packs of rice, cooking oil, and sugar at cheaper prices than minimarkets.\" data-expl=\"Indonesian household budgets dropped by 2.63% during COVID. When families are on tight budgets, they buy in bulk to save money. By using 54% centralized DC buying power, Hypermart can offer 5-kg rice bags and twin-pack cooking oil that beat minimarket prices per kilogram.\" data-source=\"AR2020 p. 48; BPS 2020 Report; Case p. 593\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s ability to serve large grocery baskets with rival buying power, weaker household spending and easy store switching.\" data-hover-reason=\"Family packs of rice and cooking oil give shoppers a lower price per unit and a reason to make a planned Hypermart trip.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-st\">ST 3</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Offer Big Family Bulk Packs on Rice and Cooking Oil</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S4, S10, T2, T3, T8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Use bulk warehouse purchasing to sell large multi-packs of rice, cooking oil, and sugar at cheaper prices than minimarkets.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"ST 4\" data-type=\"ST\" data-name=\"Team up with Lippo Ecosystem (OVO, Siloam, Lippo Malls)\" data-tags=\"S5, S9, T5, T10\" data-logos=\"hypermart,ovo,siloam,lippo\" data-desc=\"Partner with sister Lippo businesses — OVO payments, Siloam Hospitals, and Lippo residential towns — to get loyal customers without price wars.\" data-expl=\"Rivals Indomaret (Salim Group) and Alfamart have massive cash reserves to wage price wars. MPPA cannot afford price wars. Instead, Hypermart teams up with Lippo's network: supply groceries to Siloam Hospitals, offer OVO loyalty discounts, and serve Lippo township residents directly.\" data-source=\"AR2020 Note 8 & Note 33; Case p. 587\" data-hover-match=\"We matched MPPA’s retail relationships and direct customer focus with the threat from stronger rival apps and better-funded competitors.\" data-hover-reason=\"Working with OVO, Siloam and Lippo Malls could extend customer reach and share promotional costs.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-st\">ST 4</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Team up with Lippo Ecosystem (OVO, Siloam, Lippo Malls)</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[S5, S9, T5, T10]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Partner with sister Lippo businesses — OVO payments, Siloam Hospitals, and Lippo residential towns — to get loyal customers without price wars.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tows-card tows-card-wt\">\n      <div class=\"tows-card-head\">\n        <span class=\"tows-card-title\">WT Strategies (Weaknesses · Threats)</span>\n        <span class=\"tows-badge tows-badge-wt\">Mini–Mini · Retrenchment</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tows-list\">\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WT 1\" data-type=\"WT\" data-name=\"Exit Unviable Kiosks, Pilot Hy-Express &amp; Divest Wholesale\" data-tags=\"W1, W3, W5, T4, T7\" data-logos=\"hypermart,smartclub\" data-desc=\"Terminate loss-making mall kiosk leases while testing an asset-light 12–18 month 'Hy-Express' pilot in 5–6 transit nodes; liquidate SmartClub wholesale.\" data-expl=\"FMX convenience kiosks generate negligible revenue (0.7% of sales) with zero scale against 33,000 minimarkets. MPPA executes a Mini–Mini Retrenchment plan: terminate unprofitable mall leases immediately to eliminate PSAK 73 liabilities, while converting 5–6 viable transit concourses into an asset-light 'Hy-Express' pilot testing fresh RTE and digital click-and-collect. A strict 12–18 month stage-gate review determines whether to retain a transit niche or exit convenience 100%. Liquidate SmartClub wholesale to fund Hyfresh expansion.\" data-source=\"AR2020 Notes 20, 21, 38; Case Exhibit 6, p. 592\" data-hover-match=\"We matched repeated losses and heavy lease commitments with weak mall traffic and fixed rent obligations.\" data-hover-reason=\"Leaving unviable sites and selling wholesale assets can free up cash. A limited Hy-Express pilot tests the format before MPPA commits more capital.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wt\">WT 1</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Exit Unviable Kiosks, Pilot Hy-Express &amp; Divest Wholesale</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W1, W3, W5, T4, T7]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Exit loss-making kiosk leases, pilot Hy-Express in 5–6 transit hubs (12–18 mo gate), and liquidate wholesale to self-fund Hyfresh.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WT 2\" data-type=\"WT\" data-name=\"Change Fixed Mall Rent into Variable Percentage of Sales\" data-tags=\"W5, W6, T4, T7\" data-logos=\"hypermart\" data-desc=\"Renegotiate store leases with mall owners from fixed monthly rent into flexible rent based on a small percentage of monthly sales (3% to 5%).\" data-expl=\"Fixed store rent hurts MPPA badly when mall customer traffic drops by half. By changing leases to variable turnover rent (e.g., paying 3% to 5% of monthly sales), mall landlords share the pandemic traffic risk, ensuring Hypermart does not lose money during slow foot-traffic months.\" data-source=\"AR2020 Note 28; Case p. 594\" data-hover-match=\"We matched high lease costs and low sales per square meter with the risk of another drop in mall traffic.\" data-hover-reason=\"Tying rent to sales lets occupancy costs fall when revenue drops, if landlords agree to the new terms.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wt\">WT 2</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Change Fixed Mall Rent into Variable Percentage of Sales</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W5, W6, T4, T7]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Renegotiate store leases with mall owners from fixed monthly rent into flexible rent based on a small percentage of monthly sales (3% to 5%).</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WT 3\" data-type=\"WT\" data-name=\"Grow Low-Cost Private Label Brands for Rice & Essentials\" data-tags=\"W2, W7, T2, T3, T8\" data-logos=\"hypermart\" data-desc=\"Sell more in-house Hypermart private label brands for daily pantry items to give shoppers lower prices while earning higher profit margins.\" data-expl=\"Price competition pushed gross margins down to 17%. By selling Hypermart-branded sugar, rice, tissue, and cleaning products, shoppers get a 10% to 15% discount compared to major national brands, while Hypermart makes 5% higher profit margin.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 12, 54; David Ch. 6\" data-hover-match=\"We matched weak cash flow and fragmented small-store brands with price pressure from large minimarkets and tight household budgets.\" data-hover-reason=\"Affordable private-label staples can give shoppers a cheaper option while preserving more margin than repeated discounts on national brands.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wt\">WT 3</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Grow Low-Cost Private Label Brands for Rice & Essentials</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W2, W7, T2, T3, T8]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Sell more in-house Hypermart private label brands for daily pantry items to give shoppers lower prices while earning higher profit margins.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tows-item\" data-code=\"WT 4\" data-type=\"WT\" data-name=\"Stop Unprofitable Discount Wars vs Giant Minimarkets\" data-tags=\"W1, W2, T2, T9, T10\" data-logos=\"hypermart,vs,indomaret,alfamart\" data-desc=\"Stop burning cash on discount price wars against giant minimarket duopolies (Salim / Alfaria). Focus strictly on profitable fresh foods.\" data-expl=\"With a negative operating cash flow (-Rp80.4 billion), MPPA cannot win a discount price war against Salim Group (Indomaret) and Alfaria ($9.15 billion combined sales). Trying to match their prices only causes losses. MPPA must focus on fresh food and convenient online delivery where it actually makes money.\" data-source=\"AR2020 pp. 54-56; Case Exhibit 8\" data-hover-match=\"We matched recurring losses and negative operating cash flow with competitors’ greater buying power and deeper cash reserves.\" data-hover-reason=\"Ending discounts that lose money protects cash for products like fresh food where MPPA has a clearer reason for shoppers to choose it.\">\n          <div class=\"tows-item-head\">\n            <span class=\"tows-item-code tows-code-wt\">WT 4</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-name\">Stop Unprofitable Discount Wars vs Giant Minimarkets</span>\n            <span class=\"tows-item-tags\">[W1, W2, T2, T9, T10]</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"tows-item-desc\">Stop burning cash on discount price wars against giant minimarket duopolies (Salim / Alfaria). Focus strictly on profitable fresh foods.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Fred David Strategic Management Ch. 6; Case 23; Audited AR2020; Matahari.xlsx Sheet &#39;SWOT&#39;</span><span>22 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 23: Strategic Position & Action Evaluation (SPACE Matrix)",
    "short": "SPACE Matrix",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Strategy formulation · The matching stage (SPACE Matrix)</div>\n<h2>Strategic Position &amp; Action Evaluation (SPACE Matrix)</h2>\n<div class=\"space-inspector\" id=\"space-ins-box\">\n  <div class=\"space-ins-head\">\n    <span class=\"space-ins-pill space-pill-comp\" id=\"space-ins-pill\">MPPA · COMPETITIVE POSTURE</span>\n    <span class=\"space-ins-title\" id=\"space-ins-title\">Directional Vector: X = +0.60, Y = -2.80 · Competitive Quadrant (Borderline Defensive)</span>\n    <span class=\"space-ins-source\" id=\"space-ins-source\">AR2020 pp. 54–56; Case Exhibit 8; Matahari.xlsx</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"space-ins-body\" id=\"space-ins-body\">\n    <strong>Rationale:</strong> Strong food market demand (.7B) and rapid online grocery growth (+54%) offset hypermarket store drag. However, negative operating cash flow (-Rp80.4B) and heavy PSAK 73 lease financing charges (Rp166.2B) prohibit expensive debt-financed capex. MPPA must pursue asset-light delivery partnerships (GrabMart), convert space into dark stores, expand compact Hyfresh stores, and selectively retrench losing mall stores.\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"space-layout\">\n  <div class=\"space-chart-panel\">\n    <div class=\"space-panel-head\">\n      <span>Directional Vector Graph (4 Quadrants)</span>\n      <span class=\"space-chart-sub\">Origin (0,0) to Company Coordinates</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"space-svg-wrap\">\n      <svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 520\" class=\"space-svg\" id=\"space-svg-chart\">\n        <!-- Definitions -->\n        <defs>\n          <marker id=\"arrow-mppa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n            <path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 10 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#df0036\" />\n          </marker>\n          <marker id=\"arrow-alfa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n            <path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 10 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#00875a\" />\n          </marker>\n          <marker id=\"arrow-trans\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"6\" markerHeight=\"6\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n            <path d=\"M 0 1.5 L 10 5 L 0 8.5 z\" fill=\"#8b0021\" />\n          </marker>\n        </defs>\n\n        <!-- Quadrant Backgrounds -->\n        <!-- Q2 Conservative: Top-Left (-X, +Y) -->\n        <rect x=\"25\" y=\"25\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#fdfbf6\" stroke=\"#f0e5cf\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n        <text x=\"160\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#c96c00\" opacity=\"0.75\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">CONSERVATIVE</text>\n        \n        <!-- Q1 Aggressive: Top-Right (+X, +Y) -->\n        <rect x=\"300\" y=\"25\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#f2faf5\" stroke=\"#d2f0dc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n        <text x=\"440\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#00875a\" opacity=\"0.75\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">AGGRESSIVE</text>\n        \n        <!-- Q3 Defensive: Bottom-Left (-X, -Y) -->\n        <rect x=\"25\" y=\"260\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#fdf4f5\" stroke=\"#fed6db\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n        <text x=\"160\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#df0036\" opacity=\"0.75\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">DEFENSIVE</text>\n        \n        <!-- Q4 Competitive: Bottom-Right (+X, -Y) -->\n        <rect x=\"300\" y=\"260\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#f2f7fd\" stroke=\"#d5e5fc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n        <text x=\"440\" y=\"475\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#0055b8\" opacity=\"0.75\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">COMPETITIVE</text>\n        \n        <!-- Concentric Distance Reference Guides (r=2, 4, 6 units) -->\n        <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"260\" r=\"65\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0d5db\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n        <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"260\" r=\"130\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0d5db\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n        <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"260\" r=\"195\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e0d5db\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n\n        <!-- Coordinate Axes -->\n        <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"575\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#29272b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" />\n        <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"495\" stroke=\"#29272b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" />\n        \n        <!-- Origin (0,0) -->\n        <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"260\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#29272b\" />\n        <text x=\"290\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"12px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#73616c\">0,0</text>\n        \n        <!-- Axis Titles with Pill Backgrounds for Maximum Legibility -->\n        <!-- Top: +FP -->\n        <rect x=\"180\" y=\"6\" width=\"240\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n        <text x=\"300\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#0055b8\">+FP (Financial Strength)</text>\n        \n        <!-- Bottom: -SP -->\n        <rect x=\"170\" y=\"495\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n        <text x=\"300\" y=\"509\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#c96c00\">-SP (Environmental Instability)</text>\n        \n        <!-- Right: +IP -->\n        <rect x=\"420\" y=\"249\" width=\"165\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n        <text x=\"502\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#00875a\">+IP (Industry Strength)</text>\n        \n        <!-- Left: -CP -->\n        <rect x=\"15\" y=\"249\" width=\"195\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1\" />\n        <text x=\"112\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#df0036\">-CP (Competitive Disadvantage)</text>\n        \n        <!-- Vector 1: Alfamart (X = +3.80, Y = +3.00) -->\n        <g class=\"space-vector-group space-group-alfamart is-dimmed-vector\" data-company=\"alfamart\" title=\"Click to inspect Alfamart\">\n          <line class=\"space-vector-line line-alfa\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"418\" y2=\"167\" stroke=\"#00875a\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-alfa)\" />\n          <circle cx=\"423\" cy=\"163\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#00875a\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" class=\"space-chart-node space-node-alfa\" />\n          <rect class=\"space-label-bg bg-alfa\" x=\"345\" y=\"116\" width=\"205\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#00875a\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" />\n          <image href=\"/assets/alfamart-logo.svg\" xlink:href=\"/assets/alfamart-logo.svg\" x=\"353\" y=\"121\" width=\"72\" height=\"26\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" />\n          <line x1=\"433\" y1=\"122\" x2=\"433\" y2=\"146\" stroke=\"#c2ebd0\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" />\n          <text class=\"space-label-text text-alfa\" x=\"490\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#00875a\">[+3.8, +3.0]</text>\n        </g>\n        \n        <!-- Vector 2: Transmart (X = -1.60, Y = -3.60) -->\n        <g class=\"space-vector-group space-group-transmart is-dimmed-vector\" data-company=\"transmart\" title=\"Click to inspect Transmart\">\n          <line class=\"space-vector-line line-trans\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"252\" y2=\"370\" stroke=\"#8b0021\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-trans)\" />\n          <circle cx=\"248\" cy=\"377\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8b0021\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" class=\"space-chart-node space-node-trans\" />\n          <rect class=\"space-label-bg bg-trans\" x=\"50\" y=\"360\" width=\"205\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8b0021\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" />\n          <image href=\"/assets/transmart-logo.svg\" xlink:href=\"/assets/transmart-logo.svg\" x=\"58\" y=\"368\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" />\n          <line x1=\"146\" y1=\"366\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"390\" stroke=\"#fed6db\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" />\n          <text class=\"space-label-text text-trans\" x=\"196\" y=\"383\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#8b0021\">[-1.6, -3.6]</text>\n        </g>\n\n        <!-- Vector 3: MPPA (Hypermart) (X = +0.60, Y = -2.80) - Primary Highlight -->\n        <g class=\"space-vector-group space-group-mppa is-active-vector\" data-company=\"mppa\" title=\"Click to inspect MPPA\">\n          <line class=\"space-vector-line line-mppa\" x1=\"300\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"343\" stroke=\"#df0036\" stroke-width=\"5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-mppa)\" />\n          <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"351\" r=\"9.5\" fill=\"#df0036\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" class=\"space-chart-node space-node-mppa\" />\n          <rect class=\"space-label-bg bg-mppa\" x=\"330\" y=\"333\" width=\"220\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#df0036\" stroke-width=\"2\" />\n          <image href=\"/assets/hypermart-logo.png\" xlink:href=\"/assets/hypermart-logo.png\" x=\"338\" y=\"338\" width=\"74\" height=\"26\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" />\n          <line x1=\"420\" y1=\"339\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"363\" stroke=\"#fed6db\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" />\n          <text class=\"space-label-text text-mppa\" x=\"476\" y=\"356\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#df0036\">[+0.60, -2.80]</text>\n        </g>\n      </svg>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"space-breakdown-panel\">\n    <div class=\"space-panel-head\">\n      <div class=\"space-panel-title-group\">\n        <span id=\"space-breakdown-title\">Strategic Dimensions Breakdown</span>\n        <span class=\"space-chart-sub\" id=\"space-breakdown-sub\">MPPA (Hypermart) · Competitive Posture</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"space-company-selector\" role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Select company to analyze\">\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"space-comp-btn is-active\" data-company=\"mppa\" id=\"btn-space-mppa\" title=\"Click to inspect MPPA\">\n          <img src=\"/assets/hypermart-logo.png\" alt=\"Hypermart\" style=\"height:13px;max-width:34px;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:3px;\">\n          <span>MPPA</span>\n        </button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"space-comp-btn\" data-company=\"alfamart\" id=\"btn-space-alfamart\" title=\"Click to inspect Alfamart\">\n          <img src=\"/assets/alfamart-logo.svg\" alt=\"Alfamart\" style=\"height:12px;max-width:34px;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:3px;\">\n          <span>Alfamart</span>\n        </button>\n        <button type=\"button\" class=\"space-comp-btn\" data-company=\"transmart\" id=\"btn-space-transmart\" title=\"Click to inspect Transmart\">\n          <img src=\"/assets/transmart-logo.svg\" alt=\"Transmart\" style=\"height:10px;max-width:40px;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:3px;\">\n          <span>Transmart</span>\n        </button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"space-dimensions-grid\">\n      <div class=\"space-dim-card space-card-fp\" id=\"space-card-fp\" data-dim=\"FP\" data-name=\"Financial Position (FP)\">\n        <div class=\"dim-head\">\n          <strong>Financial Position (FP)</strong>\n          <span class=\"dim-score dim-score-fp\" id=\"dim-score-fp\">+1.80</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"dim-table\" id=\"dim-table-fp\">\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-fp\" data-factor=\"fp_0\"><span>Current Ratio</span><strong id=\"dim-val-fp-0\">2.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-fp\" data-factor=\"fp_1\"><span>Debt to Equity</span><strong id=\"dim-val-fp-1\">1.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-fp\" data-factor=\"fp_2\"><span>Net Income</span><strong id=\"dim-val-fp-2\">1.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-fp\" data-factor=\"fp_3\"><span>Revenue Growth</span><strong id=\"dim-val-fp-3\">2.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-fp\" data-factor=\"fp_4\"><span>Inventory Turnover</span><strong id=\"dim-val-fp-4\">3.0</strong></div>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"dim-range\">Scale: +1 (worst) to +7 (best) · Internal</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"space-dim-card space-card-cp\" id=\"space-card-cp\" data-dim=\"CP\" data-name=\"Competitive Position (CP)\">\n        <div class=\"dim-head\">\n          <strong>Competitive Position (CP)</strong>\n          <span class=\"dim-score dim-score-cp\" id=\"dim-score-cp\">-3.20</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"dim-table\" id=\"dim-table-cp\">\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-cp\" data-factor=\"cp_0\"><span>Market Share</span><strong id=\"dim-val-cp-0\">-5.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-cp\" data-factor=\"cp_1\"><span>Product Quality</span><strong id=\"dim-val-cp-1\">-2.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-cp\" data-factor=\"cp_2\"><span>Customer Loyalty</span><strong id=\"dim-val-cp-2\">-4.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-cp\" data-factor=\"cp_3\"><span>Variety of Products</span><strong id=\"dim-val-cp-3\">-2.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-cp\" data-factor=\"cp_4\"><span>Control over Suppliers</span><strong id=\"dim-val-cp-4\">-3.0</strong></div>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"dim-range\">Scale: -1 (best) to -7 (worst) · Internal</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"space-dim-card space-card-ip\" id=\"space-card-ip\" data-dim=\"IP\" data-name=\"Industry Position (IP)\">\n        <div class=\"dim-head\">\n          <strong>Industry Position (IP)</strong>\n          <span class=\"dim-score dim-score-ip\" id=\"dim-score-ip\">+3.80</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"dim-table\" id=\"dim-table-ip\">\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-ip\" data-factor=\"ip_0\"><span>Growth Potential</span><strong id=\"dim-val-ip-0\">5.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-ip\" data-factor=\"ip_1\"><span>Financial Stability</span><strong id=\"dim-val-ip-1\">4.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-ip\" data-factor=\"ip_2\"><span>Ease of Entry</span><strong id=\"dim-val-ip-2\">4.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-ip\" data-factor=\"ip_3\"><span>Resource Utilization</span><strong id=\"dim-val-ip-3\">3.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-ip\" data-factor=\"ip_4\"><span>Profit Potential</span><strong id=\"dim-val-ip-4\">3.0</strong></div>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"dim-range\">Scale: +1 (worst) to +7 (best) · External</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"space-dim-card space-card-sp\" id=\"space-card-sp\" data-dim=\"SP\" data-name=\"Stability Position (SP)\">\n        <div class=\"dim-head\">\n          <strong>Stability Position (SP)</strong>\n          <span class=\"dim-score dim-score-sp\" id=\"dim-score-sp\">-4.60</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"dim-table\" id=\"dim-table-sp\">\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-sp\" data-factor=\"sp_0\"><span>Rate of Inflation</span><strong id=\"dim-val-sp-0\">-4.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-sp\" data-factor=\"sp_1\"><span>Technological Changes</span><strong id=\"dim-val-sp-1\">-5.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-sp\" data-factor=\"sp_2\"><span>Price Elasticity</span><strong id=\"dim-val-sp-2\">-4.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-sp\" data-factor=\"sp_3\"><span>Competitive Pressure</span><strong id=\"dim-val-sp-3\">-6.0</strong></div>\n          <div class=\"dim-table-row dim-row-sp\" data-factor=\"sp_4\"><span>Barriers to Entry</span><strong id=\"dim-val-sp-4\">-4.0</strong></div>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"dim-range\">Scale: -1 (best) to -7 (worst) · External</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"space-summary-callout\">\n      <div class=\"space-vector-box\">\n        <span class=\"vec-title\">Vector Calculation</span>\n        <strong id=\"space-calc-x\">X = IP (3.80) + CP (-3.20) = +0.60</strong>\n        <strong id=\"space-calc-y\">Y = FP (1.80) + SP (-4.60) = -2.80</strong>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"space-vector-meaning\">\n        <span class=\"vec-title\">Strategic Posture &amp; Diagnosis</span>\n        <strong class=\"space-vector-heading\" id=\"space-posture-heading\">Competitive Quadrant (Borderline Defensive):</strong>\n        <p id=\"space-posture-desc\">MPPA has viable product advantages in an expanding essential grocery market, but lacks the balance sheet strength to fund heavy capital investments. Recovery must prioritize low-capital digital partnerships (GrabMart), dark-store repurposing, and closing unprofitable mall stores.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"deck-footer\"><span>Sources: Fred David Strategic Management Ch. 6; Case 23; Audited AR2020; Matahari.xlsx Sheet &#39;SPACE&#39;</span><span>23 / 30</span></div>"
  },
  {
    "label": "Slide 24: Boston Consulting Group (BCG) Matrix",
    "short": "BCG Matrix",
    "html": "<div class=\"deck-kicker\">Strategy formulation · The matching stage (BCG Matrix)</div>\n<h2>Boston Consulting Group (BCG) Matrix</h2>\n<div class=\"bcg-inspector\" id=\"bcg-ins-box\">\n  <div class=\"bcg-ins-head\">\n    <span class=\"bcg-ins-pill bcg-pill-risk\" id=\"bcg-ins-pill\">PORTFOLIO IMBALANCE · SEVERE MATURITY RISK</span>\n    <span class=\"bcg-ins-title\" id=\"bcg-ins-title\">96.7% of MPPA Revenues Concentrated in Dogs</span>\n    <span class=\"bcg-ins-source\" id=\"bcg-ins-source\">Case 23 pp. 590–592; AR2020; Matahari.xlsx Sheet &#39;BCG&#39;</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"bcg-ins-body\" id=\"bcg-ins-body\">\n    <strong>Rationale:</strong> MPPA&#39;s corporate cash generation relies almost entirely (84.2%) on Hypermart (RMSP 0.41, IGR -12.0%), which is trapped in the Dog quadrant alongside Foodmart (10.5%) and SmartClub (2.0%). Growth opportunities (Hyfresh +10%, Boston +14%) represent only 4.7% of sales, demanding immediate capital reallocation from downsizing large stores to fund compact formats.\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"bcg-layout\">\n  <div class=\"bcg-chart-panel\">\n    <div class=\"bcg-panel-head\">\n      <div class=\"bcg-panel-title-group\">\n        <span>BCG Growth-Share Matrix (2020)</span>\n        <span class=\"bcg-chart-sub\">Bubble size = % Share of MPPA Retail Sales · 4 Fred David Quadrants</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <svg viewBox=\"-28 0 628 548\" class=\"bcg-svg\" id=\"bcg-svg-chart\">\n      <!-- Y-Axis Vertical Header: IGR -->\n      <g transform=\"rotate(-90)\">\n        <rect x=\"-440\" y=\"-24\" width=\"360\" height=\"19\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1.1\" />\n        <text x=\"-260\" y=\"-11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#1e181c\">Industry Sales Growth Rate (IGR) · High +20% ← 0.0% → -20% Low</text>\n      </g>\n      <!-- 4 Quadrants -->\n      <rect x=\"25\" y=\"25\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#f2faf5\" stroke=\"#d2f0dc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n      <text x=\"162\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#00875a\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">STARS</text>\n      <text x=\"162\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#059669\" opacity=\"0.8\">High Share · High Growth</text>\n\n      <rect x=\"300\" y=\"25\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#fffdf8\" stroke=\"#fce7c8\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n      <text x=\"437\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#b45309\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">QUESTION MARKS</text>\n      <text x=\"437\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#d97706\" opacity=\"0.8\">Low Share · High Growth</text>\n\n      <rect x=\"25\" y=\"260\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#f2f7fd\" stroke=\"#d5e5fc\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n      <text x=\"162\" y=\"476\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#0055b8\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">CASH COWS</text>\n      <text x=\"162\" y=\"456\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#0284c7\" opacity=\"0.8\">High Share · Low Growth</text>\n\n      <rect x=\"300\" y=\"260\" width=\"275\" height=\"235\" fill=\"#fdf4f5\" stroke=\"#fed6db\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" rx=\"4\" />\n      <text x=\"437\" y=\"476\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15px\" font-weight=\"900\" fill=\"#df0036\" letter-spacing=\"1px\">DOGS</text>\n      <text x=\"437\" y=\"456\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#e11d48\" opacity=\"0.8\">Low Share · Low Growth</text>\n\n      <!-- Grid reference lines -->\n      <line x1=\"162\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"162\" y2=\"495\" stroke=\"#eedde4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n      <line x1=\"437\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"437\" y2=\"495\" stroke=\"#eedde4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n      <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"147\" x2=\"575\" y2=\"147\" stroke=\"#eedde4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n      <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"372\" x2=\"575\" y2=\"372\" stroke=\"#eedde4\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\" />\n\n      <!-- Principal Axes -->\n      <line x1=\"25\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"575\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#1e181c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" />\n      <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"25\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"495\" stroke=\"#1e181c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" />\n\n      <!-- Center Origin Badge -->\n      <rect x=\"266\" y=\"249\" width=\"68\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1e181c\" />\n      <text x=\"300\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#ffffff\">0.50 | 0%</text>\n\n      <!-- Top Axis Header Pill -->\n      <rect x=\"100\" y=\"522\" width=\"400\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#d0c4cc\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" />\n      <text x=\"300\" y=\"536\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#1e181c\">Relative Market Share Position (RMSP) · High 1.0 ← 0.50 → 0.0 Low</text>\n\n      <!-- Axis Ticks (X RMSP) -->\n      <text x=\"30\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#73616c\">1.0 (High)</text>\n      <text x=\"162\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#73616c\">0.75</text>\n      <text x=\"300\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#1e181c\">0.50 (Mid)</text>\n      <text x=\"437\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#73616c\">0.25</text>\n      <text x=\"570\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#73616c\">0.0 (Low)</text>\n\n      <!-- Axis Ticks (Y IGR) -->\n      <text x=\"20\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#00875a\">+20%</text>\n      <text x=\"20\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#73616c\">+10%</text>\n      <text x=\"20\" y=\"264\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#1e181c\">0%</text>\n      <text x=\"20\" y=\"376\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#73616c\">-10%</text>\n      <text x=\"20\" y=\"489\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"10px\" font-weight=\"800\" fill=\"#df0036\">-20%</text>\n\n      <!-- DIVISION 1: Hypermart (r=48 at 346, 395) - Self-contained inside circle -->\n      <g class=\"bcg-bubble-group bcg-group-hypermart\" data-division=\"hypermart\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Hypermart: Rp5,698B (84.5%), RMSP 0.41, IGR -12%\">\n        <circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"395\" r=\"50\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#df0036\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-opacity=\"0.35\" />\n        <circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"395\" r=\"48\" fill=\"#df0036\" fill-opacity=\"0.94\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"3\" class=\"bcg-bubble-circle\" />\n        <rect x=\"312\" y=\"383\" width=\"68\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#ffffff\" />\n        <image href=\"/assets/hypermart-logo.png\" x=\"316\" y=\"386\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" />\n      </g>\n\n      <!-- DIVISION 2: Foodmart & Primo (r=18 at 519, 282) with Leader Line -->\n      <g class=\"bcg-bubble-group bcg-group-foodmart\" data-division=\"foodmart\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Foodmart & Primo: Rp689B (10.2%), RMSP 0.07, IGR -2%\">\n        <line x1=\"465\" y1=\"282\" x2=\"501\" y2=\"282\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 2\" class=\"bcg-leader-line\" />\n        <circle cx=\"519\" cy=\"282\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#d97706\" fill-opacity=\"0.88\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" class=\"bcg-bubble-circle\" />\n        <rect x=\"315\" y=\"267\" width=\"150\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#ddd2d9\" />\n        <image href=\"/assets/foodmart-logo.png\" x=\"323\" y=\"271\" width=\"134\" height=\"22\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" />\n      </g>\n\n      <!-- DIVISION 3: